Not the worst shoot 'em up I've ever played, but by far not the best either.
Good stuff:
- It's a psychedelic game, with space dinosaur skulls shooting lasers, space killing cotton candies and full-speed drilling through planets and asteroids;
Bad stuff:
- I lost interest to the game quite quickly, after an hour of gameplay, nothing new happens, enemies and obstacles just getting recombined and multiplied;
- I was only able to play in 1280x720 windowed mode;
- UI and game controlls are not very well thought of;
- Game has only one (hence boring) sound track;
Rest of the things are pretty much average: enemies, weapons, bosses, play modes, difficulty level and millions of objects on the screen...

Headphones - checked;
Night - checked;
Additional pair of pants - checked.

