Incredibly good old-school platformer, taking inspiration from NES games such as Mega Man, Super Mario Bros. 3 and DuckTales. The studio that made this, Yacht Club Games, was formed from some of the people from WayForward Games, so if you have enjoyed their platformers before then you will most likely enjoy this as well.
The gameplay is spot on, with most of your actions based around your shovel, which you can upgrade after collecting the copious amounts of loot found in each of the levels. The music is also superb from Jake Kaufman/Virt (and can be found
) and imbues the game with its nostalgic feeling. Well worth it's ~8 hour campaign if you've enjoyed other classic platforming games.
